\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Dimensional calibration of the gantry, measured on a drawn $100\times 100$\,mm square. Pass~1 corrected the whole of a 2.4\,\% error from a single measurement and overshot; pass~2 is a 0.69\,\% correction off a much smaller error and should therefore be the last. Within $\pm 0.1$\,mm on a 100\,mm side is as well as an ink line can be read with callipers, and is the stopping condition. The two sides of each pair agreed to 0.06\,mm in $X$ and 0.10\,mm in $Y$, so the 0.32\,mm difference \emph  {between} the axes is real and the two are corrected apart.}}{27}{table.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:gan-square}{{8}{27}{Dimensional calibration of the gantry, measured on a drawn $100\times 100$\,mm square. Pass~1 corrected the whole of a 2.4\,\% error from a single measurement and overshot; pass~2 is a 0.69\,\% correction off a much smaller error and should therefore be the last. Within $\pm 0.1$\,mm on a 100\,mm side is as well as an ink line can be read with callipers, and is the stopping condition. The two sides of each pair agreed to 0.06\,mm in $X$ and 0.10\,mm in $Y$, so the 0.32\,mm difference \emph {between} the axes is real and the two are corrected apart}{table.caption.29}{}}
