\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {33}{\ignorespaces The emitting loop of the G-code generator as pseudocode. \texttt  {SetPen} returns nothing at all when the pen is already in the wanted state, which is what keeps the one-way toggle motor of Section~\ref {sec:gan-pen} in step with the program's model of it; the dwell it emits on a change is the $260+90$\,ms of Table~\ref {tab:gc-config}. Fault~2 of Section~\ref {sec:gc-faults} is visible here: the draw feed is emitted before every stroke but the travel feed only once, so every travel after the first runs at the draw feed.}}{83}{figure.caption.86}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gc-emitpseudo}{{33}{83}{The emitting loop of the G-code generator as pseudocode. \texttt {SetPen} returns nothing at all when the pen is already in the wanted state, which is what keeps the one-way toggle motor of Section~\ref {sec:gan-pen} in step with the program's model of it; the dwell it emits on a change is the $260+90$\,ms of Table~\ref {tab:gc-config}. Fault~2 of Section~\ref {sec:gc-faults} is visible here: the draw feed is emitted before every stroke but the travel feed only once, so every travel after the first runs at the draw feed}{figure.caption.86}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {34}{\ignorespaces The start-up warm-up as pseudocode. The two cache-building calls are the ones that, on a miss, reach into the retired source tree and import a machine-learning library; because three writers have no cached files as delivered, that miss happens on every start, which is the defect Section~\ref {sec:system} records. Running it on a background thread is what keeps the delay off the first request, and marking each writer separately is what lets the routes that do not need a cache answer immediately.}}{84}{figure.caption.87}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sys-code-warm}{{34}{84}{The start-up warm-up as pseudocode. The two cache-building calls are the ones that, on a miss, reach into the retired source tree and import a machine-learning library; because three writers have no cached files as delivered, that miss happens on every start, which is the defect Section~\ref {sec:system} records. Running it on a background thread is what keeps the delay off the first request, and marking each writer separately is what lets the routes that do not need a cache answer immediately}{figure.caption.87}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {36}{\ignorespaces Stages of the timing chains of the two modes and the measurements still missing.}}{84}{table.caption.88}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:sys-timing}{{36}{84}{Stages of the timing chains of the two modes and the measurements still missing}{table.caption.88}{}}
